How to Update Them to the Latest Version
If you notice your versions are outdated, you can upgrade them directly from the console:
To update the legacy tool: 
Update-Module -Name PowerShellGet -Force
To install/update the modern tool: 
Install-Module -Name Microsoft.PowerShell.PSResourceGet -Force

==============
Find-Module: Searches online repositories (like the PowerShell Gallery) for tools.
Install-Module: Downloads and installs a module onto your local machine.
Update-Module: Grabs the newest version of an installed module.
Uninstall-Module Safely removes a module from your system paths.

